Free the tab tint from the highlight clip

The paint of a selected tab clips the border of the highlight to the
first rows of the tab. The clip stays in force after that border, so the
colour of the selected tab reaches those rows alone. A tab therefore
loses the tint while the highlight option and the tint option both hold
true.

The paint now drops the clip after the border of the highlight. The tint
covers the whole tab again, as it does while the highlight option holds
false. The four tab positions take the same line, and the highlight
keeps the paint of before.

The change sits on the branch work/style-paint of the local tree, as commit 14 of 21.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

